      "writtenOn": "2025-10-16T00:22:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, I think I totally misunderstood how this is supposed to work.  Now I see that `ProgressiveDecoder::decode_buf_` only covers a **single** row.\n\nI think that we should pass the whole `device_bitmap_` to the decoder (e.g. `PngDecoderDelegate::PngReadHeader` should return not only `*dst_color_type` but also `*dst_span_for_whole_image` [name TBD]).  And with this, we should get rid of `PngAskScalineBuf` and `PngFillScanlineBufCompleted` (with weird inter-procedural dependencies/requirements happening across calls to both of them + weird/unnecessary hop into `decode_buf_`).\n\n(and a bit relatedly - I see that `decode_buf_.resize` is done based on **src** properties, rather than based on the requested decoding format;  this seems wrong;  I guess that ideally I should come up with a ASAN test that triggers an OOB for G or GA PNGs when they are decoded into RGB or RGBA)\n\nI will trying doing the above in a separate CL.",
